Prompt A Create an oil painting with the focal point being a young boy in an open field, holding a kite. Build layering through the painting to create visual interest and depth. Create movement through the flowing kite and the young boy’s hair and clothes. Also add texture in the clothing and kite by adding a soft shadow and warm sunlight. Use lines through the kite string and wind-swept grass to draw the viewer’s eyes to the boy. Provide unity by combining a palette of warm blues, greens, and soft warm golden light. Add glaze over the rays of sunlight to create a more luminous effect. Create a three-dimensional surface by creating impasto through the boy’s clothes and kite. Use color blending to create a shift between highlights and shadows that gives a natural sense of volume. 
Prompt B Create a linocut print with the focal point being a young boy in an open field, holding a kite. Emphasize bold contour lines through the kite string that lead the viewer’s eyes from the boy’s hand to the kite. Add thick lines to outline the boy that make him stand out. Add a few sweeping lines through the sky to suggest wind. Create contrasts through the solid black ink and negative space. 
